NAME
       mktemp - create a file or directory with a unique name

SYNOPSIS
       mktemp [-d] [-u] [-q] [-t] [-p DIR] [--suffix=SUFF]
          [--tmpdir[=DIR]] [TEMPLATE]

DESCRIPTION
       Creates a file (or a directory with -d) with a unique
       name and prints it. The trailing X's of the template
       (at least three; default tmp.XXXXXXXXXX) become random
       letters and digits from the kernel's random source.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

